pokemon legends arceus has been such a  refreshing take on the pokemon formula  dramatically changing what we've gotten  used to over the last 25 years  introducing new elements for players to  explore i've beaten the game and am well  into the end game now and i've compiled  together some interesting things that  i've noticed during my playtime if you  have any easter eggs or anything notable  that i missed drop them in the comments  below i might even grab them and make a  part 2 of this video a quick note that  there will be spoilers from the story so  keep that in mind here are 12 things you  didn't know about pokemon legends arceus  be sure to sub to the channel and like  this video while you're at it now let's  dive in  as you progress through the campaign and  save the hasuy region's various noble  pokemon from their mysterious frenzy  you'll also come across wardens that  teach you how to use these mounts these  mounts have a variety of benefits with  the key bonus being that you'll be able  to access areas that were previously out  of reach you'll start off with the word  ear and then eventually in ursulina  basket lesion sneezler and finally a  braviary  one cool thing that you can do though is  you can swap these mounts on the fly  without having to get on and off each  time you can simply press the d-pad to  change your mount at any given moment  and if you were already on a mount and  happen to go into the water for example  you'll immediately swap being in the air  or in free fall or even near a cliff  side will also give you a button prompt  to mount the right pokemon for the  terrain  you know sometimes pokemon break out of  their pokeballs that is a sad fact of  life however there is a tight window of  time where you can immediately throw  another pokeball for a second chance  catch  the best way to secure this chance is by  keeping a pokeball at the ready as soon  as the pokemon breaks free you can toss  a ball at it before it even notices you  and either enrages or  flees animation for the pokeball is  slightly different from the og games  historically the pokeball is supposed to  shake and wobble before being caught  usually three times throughout most of  the past games in legends arceus the  pokeball will dramatically pop up in the  air and emit steam clouds  you can get a quick gauge on the catch  rate and probability of the wild pokemon  being caught based on the amount of  steam high probability catches look like  only one cloud of steam is emitted and  the ball only gives a little pop in the  air while alpha pokemon and other more  difficult to catch pokemon will emit up  to three clouds of steam with the  pokeball launching super high up  now suppose you need a nice break from  the countless quests cutscenes and all  the paris trying to murder you  in that case you can hang out with your  pokemon in the overworld but not near  wild pokemon just find a bit of free  space and throw your pokemon to spawn  out and then stay within the vicinity of  them you can even interact with them and  speak with them it's also not limited to  just one pokemon either toss out your  entire team and watch them all engage  with each other you can even have your  pokemon interact with those nearby npcs  such as the warm pool or cascune and  jubilife throw out a dust talks and see  what it does  now some areas such as the alabaster  icelands will have dynamic weather like  hail or snow storms other areas may have  rain if you need to change the weather  all you have to do is simply rest at  your camp weather can be a boon if you  have pokemon moves that match the type  but it can also be detrimental if you're  using ineffective moves for example my  typhlosion was having trouble using  effective fire moves since the area had  a lot of rain but a quick camp rest  until the rain subsided and now we're  back to our regular strength  now this is an important one because  historically any pokemon involved in a  battle would get xp once the opposing  pokemon fainted this means you would  normally get xp up to 6 times per battle  however that's all been streamlined now  and your entire team will receive a  cumulative xp total at the end of an  encounter most of your encounters will  be with wild pokemon so this is not an  issue still on the rare occasion that  you encounter a noble or battle of  trainer be sure to keep in mind that if  any of your pokemon are fainted by the  end they will not receive any xp  regardless of their contributions  throughout the battle  being poisoned paralyzed or asleep used  to be a major annoyance after a battle  ended but now all status effects are  temporary whether you use an agile  normal or strong move a status effect  will have a certain number of turns  before it wears out  using a status move again will refresh  the counter you can also overwrite  certain status effects for example  causing a burnt enemy to now be  paralyzed  maybe you're using stealth rock and you  realize wait this works more like  whirlpool or firespin from the older  games or maybe you notice that the base  power and accuracy of certain moves are  slightly different well you're right  pokemon moves have had a dramatic rework  in legends arceus for example you might  not know that pulse moves like dark  pulse dragon pulse and water pulse now  have a 100 accuracy rate and any kind of  slashing move has a high crit rate  regardless of what it is this means that  dragon claw and x scissor now benefit  from a higher crit rate chance that used  to be exclusive to a move like slash  most of these reworks make sense since  there is no pvp battling in legends  arceus some of these changes are really  awesome though self-destruct for example  no longer completely faints your pokemon  instead it deals closer to like 80  percent of self-damage and huge  destructive moves like giga impact or  hyper beam no longer require a recharge  either which is wild so you can just  unleash the move back to back moves like  rollout or outrage don't lock you into  using the same move but instead now  state that your pokemon is simply  fixated on the move meaning that using  it again will gain a damage boost but  it's not mandatory not only are the  moves some of the biggest changes with  lots of hidden traits but their  animations look sick as hell too  at some point near the end of the main  campaign you will have a choice to be  accompanied by either the diamond or  pearl clan leader as you embark on the  red chain main request depending on who  you pick that will decide which  legendary pokemon you catch first and  which you will have to battle with bombs  in a noble style boss battle in my  playthrough i picked the pearl clan and  i came face to face with palkia  eventually going back to dialga later in  the story to see that dialga actually  adopted a cool origin style form during  the noble boss battle  so if you prefer to battle palkia in  that climactic battle at the end instead  and end up using the origin ball on it  make sure that you pick the diamond clan  when given the option this way palkia  comes later regardless of who you pick  you will have the option to catch both  legendaries a first for diamond and  pearl  by default your wifi connection will be  off when playing legend's arceus be sure  to turn it on that way other players can  return your lost satchels which are  important in netting mp points  you can use the mp points later to buy  evolution stones or evolution items such  as thunderstones reaper cloths metal  coats and so much more  as you go through the game's story  you'll unlock several different  locations such as the coronet highlands  or the cobalt coastland if you save the  game and fully back out and exit you'll  be greeted by a curated menu screen the  next time you log in the classic pokemon  legends arceus logo will appear on the  right with an image on the left of the  last section of the region that your  character saved its progress in  alright this is a fun one there is a  photo booth in jubalife where you can go  in and pose for the camera even putting  on this like old timey filter lens to  give it a old-fashioned and historical  look talk to the photographer and change  your poser expression you can even get  your pokemon out there too to pose with  you and hilariously you can have your  pokemon played dead it looks pretty damn  funny simply select the option for your  pokemon as you set up the photo and  enjoy  now trust me when i say there are a lot  more things on this list that i'm saving  up for a part 2. so if you want to see  more and are interested in pokemon  legends arceus please let me know sound  off with anything you've picked up on  during your play time and i'll throw  them in a future list video meanwhile do  me a solid and check out some of our  other pokemon guides and reviews and for  everything else be sure to stay with  gamespot until next time  [Music]  you
 

